This directory is vendored from choudoufu
(https://github.com/INTENTIUS/choudoufu), internal/live/gcpsweep, at commit
9807fdc1fa595e6d425cc541e8d43d48f43dde6e (branch integration/choudoufu-engine).

Every .go file here is covered by the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0,
file by file, as its own header says (SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0). The
MPL text is at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. The rest of this repository is
Apache-2.0; MPL-2.0 is file-level, so the two sit side by side and nothing
outside this directory takes on the MPL.

Files carried unchanged: attrs.go, credentials.go, doc.go, errors.go.

Files modified for plunge (each stays MPL-2.0):

  client.go   reads the marker keys from plunge's markers package
              (markers.TagStack, markers.TagURN) in place of choudoufu's
              tofu-estate and tofu-address. plunge's label values are
              digests (pkg/backend/plunge/markers), so the estate and
              address a caller passes are those digests.
  plunge.go   new: the marker key binding above; HTTPClient for the
              per-service listers; and, for INTENTIUS/plunge#42,
              NewWithHTTPClient, RefusedMarks and SourceCaller, so plunge
              can hand the sweep a client whose credential it built (no
              token source that reaches Google's auth endpoints when the
              stack names emulator endpoints).

Not carried: every _test.go file. The testdata README is not carried.
